### Token Exchange – Bearer subject (no DPoP bridging)
# @name token_exchange_bearer
POST https://localhost:5001/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Authorization: Basic {{base64(client_id:client_secret)}}

grant_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange&
subject_token={{SUBJECT_ACCESS_TOKEN}}&
subject_token_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:access_token&
audience={{TARGET_AUD}}&
scope={{REQUESTED_SCOPES}}

### Token Exchange – DPoP same-key (ath bound)
# @name token_exchange_dpop
POST https://localhost:5001/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
DPoP: {{DPoP_PROOF}}
Authorization: Basic {{base64(client_id:client_secret)}}

grant_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange&
subject_token={{SUBJECT_ACCESS_TOKEN}}&
subject_token_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:access_token&
audience={{TARGET_AUD}}&
scope={{REQUESTED_SCOPES}}

### Notes
# - Compute DPoP proof with the same key that bound the SUBJECT_ACCESS_TOKEN (same jkt) and include ath = base64url(SHA-256(subject_token)).
# - When OboDpopMode is RequireSameJkt or AllowSameJktOnly, the server will enforce same jkt and validate ath.
# - Adjust host/port to your WebAuth app.
